{"type":"standard","title":"Brandon Gill","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Brandon Gill</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q124753679","titles":{"canonical":"Brandon_Gill","normalized":"Brandon Gill","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Brandon Gill</span></span>"},"pageid":76284728,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Brandon_Gill%2C_official_portrait%2C_119th_Congress.jpg/330px-Brandon_Gill%2C_official_portrait%2C_119th_Congress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":413},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/76/Brandon_Gill%2C_official_portrait%2C_119th_Congress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":3360,"height":4200},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1374409257","tid":"565060f2-ae2f-11f1-943d-f7c17cd48628","timestamp":"2026-09-11T22:22:56Z","description":"American politician (born 1994)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brandon_Gill","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brandon_Gill?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brandon_Gill?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Brandon_Gill"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brandon_Gill","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Brandon_Gill","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brandon_Gill?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Brandon_Gill"}},"extract":"Brandon Gene Gill is an American politician, media proprietor, and former investment banker serving as the U.S. representative for Texas's 26th congressional district since 2025. A member of the Republican Party, he is the youngest Republican member of Congress. His district is anchored in Denton County, a suburban county north of Dallas and Fort Worth.","extract_html":"<p><b>Brandon Gene Gill</b> is an American politician, media proprietor, and former investment banker serving as the U.S. representative for Texas's 26th congressional district since 2025. A member of the Republican Party, he is the youngest Republican member of Congress. His district is anchored in Denton County, a suburban county north of Dallas and Fort Worth.</p>"}